# Milestone: M6
# Covers: Phase 5 (T55, T56, T59) — .new() and .clone() semantics + COW
# on derived + atom .new() returning self (S-atom-clone-perf).
#
# T39 idiom: Foo.new() is shorthand for Foo.clone() at v1.0.  Both yield
# a fresh UObject with Foo as its sole proto entry.  The COW path in
# urbi_slot_set_slow installs writes locally on the derived without
# disturbing the source.
#
# Each REPL line frames a single result; we use `;` to chain setup off
# the same line so the only framed value is the asserted one.

# .new() returns a fresh clone resolving slots through the proto chain.
var p = Object.clone(); p.setSlot("x", 42); var a = p.new(); a.x
[00000000] 42

# .new() and .clone() produce equivalent results (T55 equivalence test).
var p2 = Object.clone(); p2.setSlot("x", 42); var b = p2.clone(); b.x
[00000001] 42

# Derived can override; source unchanged (T56 COW through .new()).
var p3 = Object.clone(); p3.setSlot("x", 42); var c = p3.new(); c.setSlot("x", 99); c.x
[00000002] 99

var p4 = Object.clone(); p4.setSlot("x", 42); var d = p4.new(); d.setSlot("x", 99); p4.x
[00000003] 42

# Atom .new() returns the same atom (T59 / S-atom-clone-perf).
1.new()
[00000004] 1

"foo".new()
[00000005] "foo"
